/*!
    \module QtRos2
    \title Qt ROS2 Module
    \qtcmakepackage QtRos2
    \brief Provides Qt and QML integration with ROS 2 (Robot Operating System).

    Qt ROS2 Bridge enables Qt applications to communicate with ROS 2 nodes
    by publishing and subscribing to topics, calling services, and sending
    action goals — all from C++ or QML.

    \section1 Getting Started

    Include the core module in your CMakeLists.txt:

    \code
    find_package(QtRos2 REQUIRED COMPONENTS Core)
    target_link_libraries(my_target QtRos2::Core)
    \endcode

    Declare a ROS 2 context and nodes in QML:

    \qml
    import QtRos2.Core

    Context {}

    Node {
        nodeName: "my_qt_node"
    }
    \endqml
*/

/*!
    \page qtros2-index.html
    \title Qt ROS2
    \brief Qt and QML integration with ROS 2.

    Qt ROS2 Bridge connects Qt/QML applications to a running ROS 2 graph.
    It provides publisher and subscriber types for every ROS 2 message type,
    service clients, and action clients — all usable directly in QML.

    \section1 Guides

    \list
        \li \l{Choosing Sensor Message Types}
        \li \l{Teleoperation and Remote Control}
    \endlist

    \section1 Reference

    \list
        \li \l{Qt ROS2 QML Types}
    \endlist
*/

